PowPowPow =E2=80=94 GitHub Peer Review + Canonical Dev Instructions

Repo reviewed: prx0r/powpowpow
Review date: 19 Sep 2026
Executive conclusion

The thesis is strong and the repo already contains the right conceptual
primitives: point-in-time collection, irreversible-feed prioritization,
resource/supplier modeling, provenance, bitemporal timestamps,
recoverability, and a product flywheel from observe =E2=86=92 decide =E2=86=
=92 execute =E2=86=92
receipt.

The codebase is not yet a reliable data garden. It is currently two
overlapping implementations:

   1. Original prototype stack: warehouse.py, schema.py, v1_pipeline.py,
   old collectors, api.py, pressure/ML files.
   2. Newer P0 archival stack: core.py, quality.py, updated v1_registry.py,
   partially migrated collectors.

Do NOT add more coins, dashboards, ML, content, or execution yet. First
collapse the repo to one trustworthy ingestion/lineage system and prove one
end-to-end historical-state pipeline.

Core invariant:

Every derived fact must be reproducible from immutable raw bytes plus a
versioned transformation.

If that is not true, it is not yet PowPowPow data.
1. Critical findings P0-1 =E2=80=94 raw archive is not lossless

core.py currently stores raw_payload as only the first 10,000 characters.

That destroys exact source responses above 10 KB. The hash is calculated
from the full body, while the archived body is truncated, so the stored
artifact cannot reproduce or validate the object whose hash it claims to
represent.

Fix immediately:

   - store exact response bytes untruncated;
   - compress large responses;
   - use content-addressed blob storage where useful;
   - store metadata + hash + raw URI separately.

Never truncate raw input.
P0-2 =E2=80=94 lineage is designed but usually broken

store_normalized() accepts raw_event_id, but fetch_json() returns only
parsed data. Collectors therefore cannot naturally connect:

raw observation =E2=86=92 normalized row =E2=86=92 exact source observation

Change the transport contract so fetch_json() returns a structured
FetchResult containing:

   - observation_id
   - observed_at
   - received_at
   - source_id
   - status
   - raw_uri
   - payload_hash
   - parsed payload

Every normalizer must require one or more observation IDs.
P0-3 =E2=80=94 bitemporal time exists in schema, not yet consistently in da=
ta

The P0 commit correctly introduced event_time + observed_at, but
fetch_json() generally stores event_time =3D null and current collectors
rarely extract source time.

Canonical times:

   - event_time: on-chain/exchange/source time
   - observed_at: when collection began
   - received_at: when response/message arrived
   - normalized_at: transformation time

Ban ambiguous generic timestamp fields from canonical models.

If a source truly has no event time, leave it null and record
observation_only time semantics. Never silently substitute observed time.
P0-4 =E2=80=94 collector migration is incomplete

The latest P0 commit changed core.py, quality.py, v1_registry.py and
clore_collector.py.

Key collectors still use old direct requests wrappers and warehouse.py:

   - QUBIC
   - PRL
   - XMR
   - SafeTrade L2
   - Gate
   - CoinEx

Rule: no collector may call requests/httpx/websocket/RPC/GraphQL/gRPC
directly outside the canonical transport layer.

Delete duplicate fetch helpers after migration.
P0-5 =E2=80=94 provenance type can be false

core.py hard-codes source_type =3D rest inside the raw archive. Legacy
wrappers also discard important event semantics.

Preserve:

   - transport_type: rest | websocket | json_rpc | grpc | graphql | git |
   file
   - event_type: trade | depth_delta | depth_snapshot | block | tick |
   provider_snapshot etc.
   - source_role: canonical | secondary | enrichment | benchmark
   - source_id
   - source/protocol version when available.

P0-6 =E2=80=94 SafeTrade L2 is not gap-safe

collectors/l2_archival.py still lacks the protections already demanded by
pr1.md:

   - exchange event timestamp
   - receive timestamp
   - update/sequence ID
   - snapshot-vs-delta flag
   - gap detection
   - periodic REST checkpoint
   - deterministic reconstruction
   - reconnect/resync semantics

It also uses naive local datetime.

This is one of the most irreversible feeds in the garden and should be the
strongest collector.

Acceptance test: kill the websocket for 30 seconds, reconnect, and prove
the system either reconstructs from a checkpoint or explicitly records an
unrecoverable gap. It must never silently continue a corrupted book.
P0-7 =E2=80=94 daemon.py does not actually supervise continuous collection

It launches QUBIC and PRL once; it does not reschedule them at the
configured five-minute interval.

start_normalizer() only sets a timestamp. normalize_data() is never
scheduled.

Also:

   - stdout/stderr pipes are never drained and can deadlock;
   - no child restart supervision;
   - no exponential backoff;
   - no persisted scheduler state;
   - no PID file although health.py expects one;
   - multiple config intervals are unused.

Replace it with a real scheduler/supervisor.
P0-8 =E2=80=94 current backtest export is not a backtest dataset

export_backtest_dataset() merges current cross-sectional factor/economics
CSVs by symbol. It does not create historical point-in-time rows, forward
returns, experiment versions or walk-forward splits.

Canonical backtest rows should include:

   - as_of_time
   - network_id
   - metric_version
   - signal_definition_version
   - feature_snapshot_id
   - price_at_t
   - 1d/7d/30d/90d forward returns
   - max adverse excursion
   - BTC-relative return
   - regime
   - data_available_at

All features must satisfy observed_at <=3D as_of_time.
P0-9 =E2=80=94 observation, signal and opinion are still collapsing togethe=
r

pressure.py and two_timescale.py contain heuristic regime rules presented
as predictions.

factors.py silently defaults sell_fraction to 0.6 when missing. That is
unacceptable for a provenance-first dataset: an assumption can appear as a
measured fact.

Enforce the ladder:

OBSERVATION
=E2=86=92 METRIC
=E2=86=92 SIGNAL
=E2=86=92 HYPOTHESIS
=E2=86=92 BACKTEST RESULT
=E2=86=92 DECISION

Assumptions belong in an explicit versioned assumption_set with references.

Move pressure/regime heuristics under experiments until reproducibly tested=
.
P0-10 =E2=80=94 documented first-party source policy is not implemented

The docs correctly specify:

   - PRL: own pearld is canonical; PearlTrack is enrichment.
   - XMR: own monerod is canonical.
   - QUBIC: official RPC/static sources first.

Current implementation:

   - PRL is PearlTrack-centric.
   - XMR uses LocalMonero + CoinGecko.
   - QUBIC still uses old transport/storage.

Bring implementation in line with the source hierarchy before more derived
metrics.
2. Structural debt to remove

There are overlapping versions of core concepts:

   - schema.py vs v1_schema.py
   - registry.py vs v1_registry.py
   - warehouse.py vs v1_pipeline.py vs core.py
   - api.py vs api/app.py vs api_v2.py
   - several custom fetch helpers
   - README 16-system universe vs V1 eight-system registry
   - old XEL/XTM/technical-indicator artifacts vs current PowPowPow thesis

Choose one canonical implementation and delete/archive the rest.

There must be exactly:

   - one registry
   - one observation model
   - one transport layer
   - one raw store
   - one normalization interface
   - one metric engine
   - one active API surface.

README is stale. pr1.md says V1 is eight systems and v1_registry.py should
be source of truth. Make that true.
3. Repository hygiene and reproducibility

The repo currently contains generated bytecode/data artifacts such as:

   - *pycache* files
   - generated CSVs
   - generated JSON datasets
   - sample warehouse files
   - historical/export outputs

pr1.md already says raw history should not live in Git.

Fix:

   1. purge generated warehouse/data/bytecode from Git tracking;
   2. expand .gitignore;
   3. retain only tiny deterministic fixtures in tests/fixtures;
   4. add manifest/checksum handling for external data;
   5. never use Git as production datastore.

Add:

   - pyproject.toml
   - locked dependencies
   - explicit Python version
   - package/CLI entry points
   - environment-based config
   - no sys.path.insert(=E2=80=9C/home/box/powpowpow=E2=80=9D)
   - no hard-coded /home/box paths.

4. Target architecture

Refactor toward:
src/powpowpow/ config.py ids.py registry.py models/ observation.py
normalized.py metric.py hypothesis.py experiment.py receipt.py transport/
http.py websocket.py jsonrpc.py grpc.py storage/ raw.py parquet.py
catalog.py collectors/ safetrade.py clore.py qubic.py prl.py xmr.py
normalize/ market.py qubic.py prl.py xmr.py metrics/ miner_economics.py
resource_premium.py supply_elasticity.py subsidy_dependence.py
opportunity_cost.py signals/ definitions.py backtest/ dataset.py
event_study.py runner.py quality/ telemetry.py gaps.py freshness.py api/
mcp/ tests/ fixtures/ unit/ integration/

Recommended local-first storage:

Raw:

   - exact raw bytes
   - append-only
   - compressed
   - content-addressed where useful

Normalized:

   - Parquet partitioned by schema/network/date
   - PyArrow for writes
   - DuckDB for analytical queries

High-frequency L2:

   - micro-batch to Parquet every 10=E2=80=9360 seconds
   - do not write millions of individual filesystem records.

Catalog:

   - DuckDB or SQLite for source registry, collector runs, observation
   manifest, schema versions, transformations, hypotheses, backtests and
   quality incidents.

This remains cheap and VPS-friendly.
5. Canonical object model

Do not make coin the primary identity.

Use stable IDs such as:

   - network_id =3D monero-mainnet
   - asset_id =3D XMR
   - resource_id =3D randomx-cpu-hash
   - venue_id =3D safetrade
   - hardware_id =3D nvidia-rtx-4090
   - source_id =3D monerod-local

Ticker symbols are presentation metadata.

Persistent objects:

   - Source
   - Observation
   - Entity
   - Snapshot
   - Transformation
   - MetricDefinition
   - MetricValue
   - Claim
   - EvidenceEdge
   - Hypothesis
   - Experiment
   - Outcome
   - Decision
   - ExecutionReceipt
   - Feedback

Every derived object must carry:

   - definition_id
   - definition_version
   - computed_at
   - input IDs
   - code/build version
   - units
   - quality/confidence metadata where relevant.

6. Build order Milestone 0 =E2=80=94 freeze scope

No new networks.
No new dashboard.
No new ML.
No allocator/executor.
No generic sentiment/news.
No technical-analysis expansion.
Milestone 1 =E2=80=94 one ingestion kernel

Implement one transport/archive API and migrate every collector.

Definition of done:

   - no direct requests.get in collectors
   - every successful and failed request creates an observation record
   - exact raw bytes preserved
   - every normalized row has lineage
   - all times UTC-aware
   - hash round-trip tests pass.

Milestone 2 =E2=80=94 irreversible feeds first

Priority:

   1. SafeTrade L2/trades
   2. Clore/Akash/Nosana supply and pricing
   3. any other non-reconstructable resource-market feeds

Implement sequence/gap handling, reconnect policy, checkpoints and
collector-run telemetry.
Milestone 3 =E2=80=94 canonical first-party chain feeds

QUBIC:

   - official RPC
   - tick/epoch/computor history
   - emission/burn/contract events
   - exact source event times

PRL:

   - own pearld canonical collector
   - PearlTrack enrichment only
   - classification_source/version/confidence on labels

XMR:

   - own monerod
   - block/difficulty/emission/fee/security-budget series
   - no fake address-flow analytics

Then QUAN/KAS.
Milestone 4 =E2=80=94 historical state layer

Create deterministic:

   - resource_state
   - network_state
   - market_state
   - supplier_state
   - hardware_state

Each snapshot includes event/valid time, observation time, lineage, schema
version and quality state.

This is the actual garden.
Milestone 5 =E2=80=94 versioned metrics

Start only with:

   - miner margin
   - resource premium
   - subsidy dependence
   - supply elasticity
   - issuance pressure
   - liquidity-adjusted miner pressure
   - compute opportunity cost

Metric runs must be reproducible from IDs.
Milestone 6 =E2=80=94 hypothesis/backtest engine

Explicit hypothesis example:
HYP_MINER_PRESSURE_001 statement: elevated miner pressure predicts lower 7d
BTC-relative return metric_definition: miner_pressure_v1 horizon: 7d

Backtester outputs:

   - occurrence count
   - 1d/7d/30d/90d returns
   - BTC-relative returns
   - volatility
   - max adverse excursion
   - regime slices
   - confidence intervals
   - walk-forward result
   - exact dataset/version hash.

No bullish/bearish score unless a tested mapping defines the number.
Milestone 7 =E2=80=94 read-only API and real MCP

Current mcp_server.py is a tool manifest/dispatcher, not a full MCP
transport server.

After warehouse integrity is proven, expose:

   - pow_get_state
   - pow_get_metric
   - pow_explain_metric
   - pow_get_evidence
   - pow_compare_resource_routes
   - pow_get_hypothesis
   - pow_run_backtest
   - pow_get_data_quality

Every response returns provenance IDs.

Current api.py caches JSON at process import and can serve stale data
forever. Replace with dynamic queries against canonical current state.
Milestone 8 =E2=80=94 content

Content is downstream.

Generate from:

   - largest state changes
   - historical extremes
